model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "Bulk metadata import accepts only the recorded pool owner through the typed owner-session route. Host policy transactions finish before backend calls; a signed short-lived callback rechecks current ownership, organization membership and app-management permission before every chunk. Upload never approves execution. Exact descriptor and canonical map digests bind approval, source identities and attribution. The dedicated EU job uses immutable EU record-storage chunks, fresh scoped Home row locks and additive model-history v6 job/receipt tables. Each adaptive SQL subrange commits records and its exact replay receipt together, preserves a persisted cooldown, throttles at 70 percent CPU until below 60 and stops after sustained 90 percent or database errors. Release and backup windows pause new batches. An optional serving source becomes binding once configured; its frozen per-route and stream-mode baseline never ratchets upward, and failed or stale observations pause. Status retains counts, thresholds, pacing and attention reasons. Missing model telemetry remains explicitly unavailable, never a control-duration substitute. Changed retained contents refuse. It changes no dependency or pin."
    }
  }
}
